  "conclusion": "The original M3 record and same-host warm replay initialized a FlashInfer mnnvl workspace. Both old M4 cold replays and the new cold replay failed mnnvl initialization with CUDA_ERROR_ILLEGAL_STATE and initialized trtllm instead. Therefore each cold replay comparison changes an unrecorded collective workspace subbackend relative to the record. Per-call FlashInfer dispatch was not traced, so this is a material unresolved confound, not proof that either backend caused the observed tensor differences.",
