  "hypotheses_not_cause_claims": [
    "The GPU-pair topology or exposed NVSwitch multicast capability may differ across instances despite matching H100 model, driver and VBIOS.",
    "A CUDA/driver initialization-state difference may make multicast unavailable; CUDA_ERROR_ILLEGAL_STATE and the earlier Torch symmetric-memory multicast warnings co-occur in all three trtllm-fallback logs.",
    "If eligible standalone allreduce calls dispatched through FlashInfer, mnnvl versus trtllm could change floating-point reduction order. No retained per-call dispatch trace proves that this occurred.",
    "The identical warm replay and differing cold replays correlate with both cache/process placement and collective backend, so neither factor is isolated by these observations."
  ],
  "interpretation_update": "Old M4 cold a/b and new cold followup c should be described as mnnvl-record versus trtllm-replay comparisons. Their P2=DIFFERS verdicts remain valid observations of the complete runs, but do not isolate cold-process repeatability within one collective implementation. The old M3 warm replay is mnnvl-to-mnnvl and P2=IDENTICAL, but it is same-host/warm and cannot isolate backend effects either.",
  "needed_for_isolation": [
    "Record the initialized workspace backend as a required comparison field.",
    "Add per-call dispatch counters or traces for FLASHINFER, CUSTOM, SYMM_MEM and PYNCCL; workspace initialization alone is insufficient.",
    "For a future controlled pair, force the same VLLM_FLASHINFER_ALLREDUCE_BACKEND in record and replay and fail the run if that workspace cannot initialize."
  ],
